    <string name="s486">"Connect with OBS Studio (OBS Guide)"</string>
    <string name="s487">"Browser Source · 1920×1080"</string>
    <string name="s488">"Connection links for broadcast programs (OBS / vMix / Projector):"</string>
    <string name="s489">"• For verses at the bottom of the screen (Lower Third): use link 1.\n• For the full display (Projector/Full): use link 2.\n• For maximum performance and NDI 6 quality: look for NDI sources directly.\n• For old editing programs: use MJPEG link 3."</string>
    <string name="s490">"How to connect with OBS Studio (5 quick steps):"</string>
    <string name="s491">"1. In OBS, click the (+) button in the Sources section and choose Browser."</string>
    <string name="s492">"2. Put the link above in the URL field: %1$s."</string>
    <string name="s493">"3. Set the dimensions: Width = 1920 and Height = 1080."</string>
    <string name="s494">"4. Make sure the (Shutdown source when not active) option is selected."</string>
    <string name="s495" formatted="false">"5. As soon as you tap any verse in the app, it appears immediately in the live broadcast with a 100% transparent background over the camera!"</string>
    <string name="s496">"Connect with vMix (vMix Guide)"</string>
    <string name="s497">"Web Browser input · SetText push"</string>
    <string name="s498">"How to connect with vMix:"</string>
    <string name="s499">"1. In vMix, click Add Input at the bottom of the screen."</string>
    <string name="s500">"2. Choose the Web Browser tab from the side menu (or the Stream / VLC tab and use the live stream link)."</string>
    <string name="s501">"3. Paste the feed link, and set the resolution to 1920x1080."</string>
    <string name="s502">"4. Link the input to one of the Overlay channels (1, 2 or 3) to merge the verses with automatic alpha transparency."</string>
